      "sha256": "c7229fd114f6cb7cdb53caa8f31f68f41b84067412db74d20c208c36e5f4f0d8",
      "identification": "Safemon Gh0st-derived RAT/rootkit installer",
      "judgement": "MALICIOUS",
      "static_evidence": [
        "The GUI PE carries and stages a kernel rootkit plus a Gh0st-derived surveillance DLL. Concrete directory-result hiding, BIOS boot-code hooking, keystroke recording, and clipboard capture establish malicious behavior independently of its collection name.",
        "Outer main at 0x401c30 invokes VM-process enumeration (0x401870), driver staging (0x401450/0x4015b0), driver activation, and rundll32.exe safemon.dll hook2. 0x401505 writes the embedded 0x49600-byte driver from VA 0x40dc50.",
        "Kernel PE at file offset 0xba50: syscall target lookup at VA 0x11524 reads the service index and KeServiceDescriptorTable; interceptors at 0x13d7e and 0x13f74 substitute handlers. The query-directory filter compacts linked records to omit selected results.",
        "Embedded 16-bit boot code in the driver reduces conventional memory and relocates itself; offset 0x6c18 replaces the INT 13 vector, and 0x6cfe patches matching boot code with an operand-size-prefixed far call to its relocated payload.",
        "Surveillance DLL at file offset 0x147d8: VA 0x1000e366 polls GetAsyncKeyState and tests bit 0x8000. Foreground-window context and key labels feed 0x1000e050, whose loop XORs bytes by 0x62 and writes them at 0x1000e14f. 0x10010a6c requests CF_TEXT, copies locked clipboard data into a 0x77-tagged record and hands it to the transport at 0x10010b09.",
        "Purpose/deployment: class RTTI and exports corroborate Gh0st lineage, but the verdict rests on the recording, rootkit and boot-hook code. No authorized administration or forensics deployment context is available. Static capability is established; installation success is unproven."
      ],
