      "sha256": "2dd6e6afcd252b7df79a9866ec2a37fec90cb39911a1f41b52fadee8b9c06128",
      "identification": "StormAttack service/injection loader and packet-tasked DDoS implant",
      "judgement": "MALICIOUS",
      "static_evidence": [
        "The native loader replaces service DLL configuration, registers Active Setup, injects a DLL, and carries a remotely tasked raw-packet flood implant. These are concrete abuse mechanisms, not an ordinary network diagnostic tool.",
        "Outer 0x401150 creates a process, allocates remote storage, writes a DLL path and starts a remote thread using resolved LoadLibraryA. 0x401390 resolves a DLL export for an additional remote-thread handoff. Other paths bind persistence writes to LanmanServer ServiceDLL and Active Setup StubPath and construct shell cleanup.",
        "Embedded PE at file offset 0x5060: 0x10006ac9 is the packet task handler. recv at 0x10006b45 fills a record copied at 0x10006b6f; its first DWORD selects flood modes, downloads/launches, or disruptive commands.",
        "0x100022b6 calls WSASocketA(AF_INET, SOCK_RAW, IPPROTO_UDP). The loop at 0x10002353 issues twelve sendto calls per burst, sleeps and repeats until stopped. Other modes build spoofed packets and HTTP requests.",
        "The command dispatcher reaches URLMon acquisition/launch helpers and shutdown helpers using SeShutdownPrivilege and ExitWindowsEx. STORM formatting, welcome/DNS banners and version identity corroborate StormAttack, not the unrelated family names in the collector filename.",
        "Purpose/deployment: no authorized stress-test context is available, and service hijacking, concealment and remote attack tasking tip the verdict. The embedded PE has no exported functions, so the outer resolved-export injection path is not proof of a working deployment. Hostile implementation remains present."
      ],
